Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 12:02:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/32] fix(desktop): browser attachments via a web file
 registry + data_url-only file.attach
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Attachments were fully broken in the web build: selectPaths rejected,
getPathForFile returned '' (so non-image drops produced no chip), images
needed saveImageBuffer, and api.upload refused outright. The renderer's
attach pipeline is path-keyed, so the fix lands at the bridge seam:

- web-file-registry: browser Files/blobs get stable virtual paths
  (/__webfs__/<id>/<name>); pure module, empty and inert under Electron
- web bridge: selectPaths drives one persistent hidden file input
  (directories reject honestly), getPathForFile/saveImageBuffer register
  bytes, readFileDataUrl resolves registry paths before the fs REST
  fallback — picks, drops, previews, and clipboard-pasted images all work
- uploadComposerAttachment: virtual paths are gateway-invisible, so
  file.attach sends {name, data_url, session_id} with NO path; the
  backend stages the bytes from data_url alone
- webApi: api.upload implemented with FormData (browser-owned multipart
  boundary), POST default, same auth/error mapping

Tests: registry round-trip + fall-through, upload FormData shape, and the
file.attach no-path contract for browser-picked files.
